Are you strong in planning, organizing, and maintaining oversight in a dynamic logistics environment? Do you enjoy improving processes while supporting a fast-growing operation? Then the role of Operations Planner in Moerdijk could be your next career move. Working in one of the largest and most modern warehouses in the Benelux, you will play a crucial role in ensuring the smooth flow of daily order operations. You will make sure everything behind the scenes is perfectly coordinated, allowing the operation to perform at its best.

As an Operations Planner, you will be responsible for the warehouse's outbound planning activities. You will ensure that customer orders are properly prepared, scheduled, and processed within the operation. Working closely with the operational teams, you will act as a key link between systems, planning, and execution.

Your responsibilities include:

- Processing daily customer requests and forecasts;
- Planning and prioritizing outbound orders within the system;
- Aligning capacity and operational activities with the warehouse floor;
- Coordinating pick-and-pack processes to ensure orders are processed efficiently;
- Acting as the first point of contact for operational planning-related questions;
- Monitoring the progress, timing, and accuracy of order flows;
- Ensuring that all process steps are followed strictly from start to finish;
- Supporting the optimization of planning and logistics processes.

For this position, we are looking for someone who excels at planning and can maintain a clear overview in a complex logistics environment.

- Relevant experience within logistics (planning and/or warehouse operations);
- Strong organizational and administrative skills;
- Ability to work under pressure and effectively prioritize tasks;
- Good command of the English language (required);
- Comfortable working with computers and digital systems;
- Available to work full-time in a two-shift schedule.

Are you technically skilled and looking for a full-time job as a process operator in Heerenveen? In this role, you will join a leading producer of margarines, oils, and fats. You will monitor the production process, ensure quality and safety, and directly contribute to customer satisfaction. Do you want to work in the food industry with excellent career opportunities and a great team atmosphere? Read on to discover your new challenge!

As a process operator, you will be responsible for running and supervising a modern production line where margarine, oils, and fats are manufactured and packaged. You will monitor the entire process, adjust machines when needed, and perform quality checks on finished products. With your technical insight and attention to detail, you make sure production runs smoothly, safely, and according to the highest quality standards.

This is a 3-shift schedule position, giving you variety in your work as well as extra free time. It’s a dynamic role with plenty of opportunities to grow and develop.

We are looking for a process operator with the following skills and qualifications:

- Technical affinity or work experience as an operator/process operator;

- Experience in a production environment, preferably in the food industry;

- Motivated, eager to learn, and detail-oriented;

- Strong focus on quality, hygiene, and safety;

- Availability for a full-time 40-hour work week;

- Willingness to work in a 3-shift schedule;

- Good command of the Dutch or English language (spoken and written).

As a Logistics Employee, you will be part of a team that keeps warehouse operations running smoothly. Depending on your experience and interests, you can work in different departments.

🔧 Tools Department

In the Tools department, you work with specialized equipment and materials.

Your tasks may include:

- Checking tools and materials;
- Scanning products into the system;
- Managing stock levels;
- Preparing materials for shipment;
- Maintaining an organized workspace.

📥 Inbound Department

As an Inbound Employee, you process incoming goods and make sure everything is stored correctly.

Your responsibilities include:

- Receiving deliveries;
- Checking products and quantities;
- Scanning goods into the system;
- Storing products in the correct warehouse locations.

📦 Outbound Department

In Outbound, you make sure customer orders are ready to leave the warehouse.

Your tasks include:

- Picking orders;
- Checking products;
- Packing shipments;
- Preparing orders for transport.

🚜 Reach Truck Positions

Do you have reach truck experience or would you like to develop these skills?

As a Reach Truck Operator, you will:

- Move products throughout the warehouse;
- Replenish stock;
- Pick orders from warehouse racks;
- Work safely at height.

Don't have a certificate yet? Olympia can help you obtain one.

- You are available to work in a 2-shift schedule;
- You speak English, Dutch, or Polish;
- You are motivated and reliable;
- You enjoy working in a team;
- Warehouse experience is a plus, but not required.

As an Electrotechnician, you will play a key role in ensuring the reliability and safety of electrical systems. You will work on installation projects, perform maintenance activities, and troubleshoot technical issues to keep operations running smoothly.

Your daily responsibilities include:

- Installing electrical systems and equipment;
- Performing preventive and corrective maintenance;
- Diagnosing and resolving electrical faults and malfunctions;
- Inspecting installations to ensure compliance with safety regulations;
- Reading and interpreting technical drawings and electrical schematics;
- Collaborating with colleagues and customers to deliver high-quality solutions.

This is a varied position where no two days are the same, offering plenty of opportunities to further develop your technical skills.

- MBO Level 3 diploma in Electrical Engineering or a comparable technical qualification;
- Minimum of 2 years of experience as an Electrotechnician;
- Valid VCA certificate or willingness to obtain one;
- Driving license B is considered an advantage;
- Good command of Dutch and/or English;
- Strong focus on safety, quality, and precision;
- Ability to work independently as well as part of a team.
